{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in deterministic specifications. The policy gives random_walk in clear exploration, inserts a one-shot forward pulse after a clear exploratory pulse to bias coverage, and routes every obstacle event through dedicated turn-recovery states. Obstacle-side states choose a consistent turn direction away from blocked space. Action states self-loop on path_clear and only obstacle events can preempt them, matching the stated runtime semantics.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion in plant automata",
    "Use one main policy specification with small helper states for one-shot exploration and obstacle recovery",
    "Make obstacle_front go to a dedicated recovery state with exactly one turning action",
    "Make obstacle_left prefer clockwise recovery and obstacle_right prefer counterclockwise recovery",
    "Use random_walk in the initial clear state and alternate back to short forward progress when safe",
    "Keep action states one-shot and return quickly to exploration after path_clear"
  ],
